Let me understand the requirements:

1. `DocumentService.archive(actor, id)` needs authorization.
2. Actor has tenant, user, role: admin, editor, viewer.
3. Only active documents in the actor's tenant are visible.
4. Missing, deleted, and foreign-tenant documents all throw `Error('not found')` — even for admin.
5. An admin may archive any visible document.
6. An editor may only archive a document they own (document.owner === actor.user).
7. A viewer may never archive.
8. Unauthorized visible requests throw `Error('forbidden')`.
9. On success: set `archived = true` and append exactly `{actor: actor.user, document: id}` to audit.
10. Repeating archive on an already archived visible document is a no-op (no new audit entry, no change), BUT still enforce permission first. So if a viewer tries to archive an already-archived visible document, it should still throw 'forbidden'. If an editor tries on an archived document they don't own — 'forbidden'. If document is archived but not visible — 'not found'.
11. Failures must leave every document and audit entry unchanged.

